"} "36 from 19 countries"]]] [:tr {:class "records", :style ""} [:th {:style "vertical-align: top;"} "Olympic Record "] [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/1111"} "1:07.18"] " " [:span {:class "label label-primary"} "WR"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/98555"} "Gerard van Velde"] " " [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"] " / 16 February 2002 / " [:a {:href "/records/event_name/531"} "Details"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Starter"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5003840"} "Ole Hermann Sørli"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5001695"} "Daniel Cabelduc"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "As in the 500 m, the ban on a large number of Russian athletes had impact on the event. Notably, Pavel Kulizhnikov and " [:a {:href "/athletes/128410"} "Denis Yuskov"] ", who had finished 1-2 at the 2016 Worlds, and had both won World Cup races in the running season, were not allowed to compete. This left two main contenders for the title: " [:a {:href "/athletes/137695"} "Kjeld Nuis"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/128235"} "Håvard Holmefjord Lorentzen"] ". Both had already won gold at the Gangneung Oval, in the 1,500 m and 500 m, respectively. Nuis was the reigning World Champion in the event, while Lorentzen led the current World Cup standings ahead of Nuis."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The track record, set by Nuis at the 2017 Worlds, was bettered in the 13th pair by " [:a {:href "/athletes/128108"} "Kim Tae-Yun"] ". Having placed 30th in the event at the 2014 Olympics, and having only occasionally placed into the international top 10, he was a virtual unknown, but his 1:08.22 moved him into an eventual bronze medal position. Lorentzen then managed to push below 1:08, helped by the fastest full lap of the field. In the final pair, Nuis opened up a tiny gap of 0.15 at the 200 m mark, and carried the advantage all the way to the finish line, leaving him with 1:07.95. Nuis thus became the third person to win gold in both 1,000 and 1,500 metres at the same Olympics, following " [:a {:href "/athletes/86551"} "Eric Heiden"] " in 1980 and " [:a {:href "/athletes/84286"} "Gaétan Boucher"] " in 1984."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button894688", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button894688').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "200 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "600 m"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "18I"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/137695"} "Kjeld Nuis"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "1:07.95"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "16.31"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "41.35"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "16I"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/128235"} "Håvard Lorentzen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]] [:td {} "1:07.99"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "16.46"] [:td {:class "split", :style